  "plain": "A podcast host, Jesse Michels, says that around late 2024 the National Science Foundation, a US government agency that funds research, and NASA, the US space agency, co-sponsored a podcast. According to Michels, it featured well-credentialed scientists and engineers looking into extended electrodynamics, an expanded version of the physics of electricity and magnetism that some link to unusual propulsion. He presents it as a sign that serious institutions are taking the idea seriously."
